0.4.0-2 | 2026-07-22 20:29:17 +0200

  * Fix flaky tests (Jaime Piña, Corelight)

    Currently, the telemetry.zeek test outputs data non-deterministically.
    This change sorts the output, so the tests pass more consistently.

    Also, waiting for 10ms for nats messages is not enough time on certain
    systems. This increases the timeout to avoid test flakes.

0.4.0 | 2026-06-26 19:10:03 +0200

  * Allow optionally creating a Stream (Jaime Piña, Corelight)

    Currently, there is hard-coded behavior to always create a JetStream
    Stream.

    This change introduces a new option called create_stream that allows a
    user to enable or disable that behavior.

0.3.1 | 2026-05-26 09:38:40 +0200

  * test: add btest for stream_subject_template per-filter config (Simon Dugas, Corelight)

    Verifies that setting stream_subject_template via a Log::Filter's
    $config table correctly overrides the global value.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

  * fix(NATS): read globals on main thread, not in DoInit (Simon Dugas, Corelight)

    DoInit runs in the writer backend thread where global_scope() is
    not safe to access. Move all zeek::id::find_val calls into the
    constructor, which executes on the main thread.

    Also fixes incorrect BoolVal casts on non-bool fields that were
    introduced alongside the original code.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

  * fix(NATS): assign stream_subject_template correctly in DoInit (Simon Dugas, Corelight)

    The stream_subject_template config key was mistakenly assigning its
    value to stream_name_template, silently clobbering it and leaving
    stream_subject_template unset.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

  * Add btest for telemetry (Arne Welzel, Corelight)

    I had this locally but never staged :-(

